{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1539878-how-powerful-are-the-earthbound","id":1539878,"title":"How powerful are the earthbound?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-05T13:20:58-07:00","id":1539878,"title":"How powerful are the earthbound?","content":"In comparison to the other game lines big bars we have the antediluvians, the wyrm, the nephandi, and the fomori. So where do the earthbound fall on this list of antagonists forces? It can be weaker earthbound, middling, or super powerful. Any examples from former games would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T16:39:12-07:00","id":1539895,"title":"","content":"Contrary to other Big Hitters, the Earthbound are a known quantity, even because becoming one is rather easy for the Fallen. All it takes is for a Demon to possess an object instead of a human. The book on Earthbounds has all their rules.<br /> <br /> Between just a couple exclusive abilities, good investments in Faith and servitors, and the normal rules for the Fallen, an Earthbound can do things like causing an earthquake to an entire continent at once, and other humongous feats of magic.<br /> <br /> Now, how this relates to the other Big Hitters is hard to say because those powerful beings are usually undefined in the rules, with good reason, and their relative power depends on who you ask and which game line you're playing.<br /> <br /> In practical terms, why would anyone cause a continental earthquake or level a city? What's the actual end goal of such beings, what are their winning conditions? What their power means in the context of Vampire? Of Werewolf? Of Mage?<br /> <br /> The Earthbound are meant in DtF to be world conquerors, trying to eliminate competition and control the Fallen to the last, eating any they can't subjugate, and The Five are there as the most powerful of their kind. Those five are either the most powerful spirits in existence, or capable of enslaving anything above them.<br /> <br /> Yet they're ultimately just Fallen, and have nothing that any other Fallen can't acquire with enough time and effort. Hence why battling competition is so important for them.<br /> <br /> All of this is only true for a regular DtF game, though. For a Werewolf game they're just powerful Incarna, even if they mostly follow DtF rules on how to stat them. The Wyrm is so much above they're probably just unwitting servants of one of its heads or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:19:16-07:00","id":1539903,"title":"","content":"One thing to keep in mind is that Earthbound can vary a lot. The average Fallen PC is already pretty powerful, but there are setting Earthbound NPCs that, due to summoning rituals or other mishaps, were brought to Earth long before the Abyss broke open,. These Earthbound would have had a lot of time to build up followers and amass faith and resources and depending on when they were summoned, may still retain a lot of the original power that the Fallen PCs are assumed to have lost.<br /> <br /> I think basically any time you see a &quot;demon&quot; in another line, like Metathiax or Kupala, we can assume that they're intended to be interpreted as Earthbound if you're playing with Demon the Fallen as part of your cosmology.<br /> <br /> There are also the Archdukes. They were Lucifer's generals and were summoned in ancient times. I might be wrong, but I don't remember them being given stats anywhere, and the assumption would be that they're probably one of those adversaries that, like the Antediluvians, are pretty assumed to be beyond measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T09:14:09-07:00","id":1540210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carsusbloodking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1539878-how-powerful-are-the-earthbound#post1539878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In comparison to the other game lines big bars we have the antediluvians, the wyrm, the nephandi, and the fomori. So where do the earthbound fall on this list of antagonists forces? It can be weaker earthbound, middling, or super powerful. Any examples from former games would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also the Neverborn Malfeans and the Oracles Mages, yes.<br /> <br /> The 5 Archdukes are at least as powerful as any one of those, if not more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}